NODE id=matrix/neo/internal/memory.Pager.FailOpportunityAttempt kind=method
  digest=b3:34398d52f36e7f917f939f0b877b021300bf19909608a0412a4bf70f8394ae1a file=neo/internal/memory/writeback.go range=532:581 lang=go exported=true byte_range=20623:22845
  sig=func (p *Pager) FailOpportunityAttempt(ctx context.Context, uri string, maxAttempts int) (OpportunityStatus, error)
  doc=FailOpportunityAttempt records a failed/partial autonomous run attempt on an\nopportunity: it increments the bounded attempts counter and re-sets the\nlifecycle status, persisted atomically as a single cortex Update (one Pebble\nbatch commit). While attempts remain under maxAttempts the opportunity is\nreturned to PENDING so a later wake can retry it; once the attempts reach the\nceiling it is DISMISSED (eventually give up rather than retry forever, req\n5.5). maxAttempts <= 0 disables the ceiling (always re-pend). Returns the new\nstatus. No user-facing surface is touched — a failed proactive attempt is\nsilent (req 5.5: no failed-surprise spam).
EDGES
  ^contains=matrix/neo/internal/memory.Pager
  ^defines=matrix/neo/internal/memory/writeback.go

NODE id=matrix/neo/internal/memory.Pager.HasEmbedder kind=method
